# Line endings for files that run under a Unix shell. A CR is a syntax error to sh and bash
# -- in a container, in CI, in a git hook -- not a cosmetic difference. Whether a checkout
# gets CRLF is otherwise decided by core.autocrlf, which differs per PC and travels with no
# clone; this file travels with the repository and outranks it.
#
# Seeded once by /apply-standards (engineering_standards/templates/.gitattributes); this
# repository owns it from then on. The `gitattributes-eol` scanner rule checks that the LF
# lines below keep resolving, so edit freely around them.
#
# Deliberately no `* text=auto`: on adoption it would renormalise the whole index in one
# commit. Whether to take that is this repository's own decision.

*.sh                             text eol=lf
Dockerfile                       text eol=lf
Dockerfile.*                     text eol=lf
*.Dockerfile                     text eol=lf

# Git hooks are shell scripts without an extension -- same hazard, no *.sh to catch them.
engineering_standards/hooks/*    text eol=lf

# cmd.exe finds `goto` / `call :label` targets reliably only in CRLF files.
*.bat                            text eol=crlf
*.cmd                            text eol=crlf
